```

### Example

```text
package name: uriel-studio
version: 0.1.0
description: A VS Code extension for authors, worldbuilders, and storytellers.
entry point: extension.js
test command:
git repository:
keywords: vscode,writing,author,markdown,worldbuilding,storytelling,lore,fantasy,novel,codex
author: Your Name
license: MIT
```

### Note

Since you're building a **VS Code extension**, the recommended starting point is actually:

```bash
npm init -y
```

followed by adding the VS Code-specific dependencies and configuration. This is typically simpler than answering all of `npm init`'s prompts interactively.
